Algorithm 1 The Ford-Fulkerson Algorithm
Input: G = (V, E), C, vs, vt.
fuv = 0 : ∀(u, v) ∈E
while ∃augmenting path P = {vs, . . . , vt} in G do :
cp = min{cuv : (u, v) ∈P} ;
for each (u, v) ∈P do:
fuv = fuv −cp;
fvu = fvu + cp;
cuv = cuv −cp;
cvu = cvu + cp;
end for
end while
